.TH start-registry-os-version-edit 1  "edit " 
.SH NAME
start\-registry\-os\-version\-edit \- Edit OS version metadata; omitted fields remain unchanged
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBstart\-registry os version edit\fR [\fB\-\-release\-notes\fR] [\fB\-\-source\-version\fR] [\fB\-\-git\-hash\fR] [\fB\-\-expected\-git\-hash\fR] [\fB\-\-security\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIVERSION\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Edit OS version metadata; omitted fields remain unchanged
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-release\-notes\fR \fI<RELEASE_NOTES_OR_JSON>\fR
Release notes for this version
.TP
\fB\-\-source\-version\fR \fI<SOURCE_VERSION>\fR
Source version range for migration
.TP
\fB\-\-git\-hash\fR \fI<GIT_HASH>\fR
Git commit that built the OS release
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-git\-hash\fR \fI<EXPECTED_GIT_HASH>\fR
Reject the operation if the indexed OS commit has changed
.TP
\fB\-\-security\fR \fI<SECURITY>\fR
Mark the OS release as a security update
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
true
.IP \(bu 2
false
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIVERSION\fR>
StartOS version number
